---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const P1 = `function areaOf(width, height)
{
  return width * height;
}

let a = areaOf(5, 3);
console.log(a);`;
const P2 = `PROCEDURE twice(n)
{
  RETURN(n * 2)
}

x ← twice(6)
DISPLAY(x)
DISPLAY(twice(x))`;
const P3 = `function label(name, score)
{
  console.log(name + ": " + score);
}

label("Avery", 88);`;
const RefCard = `PROCEDURE procName(p1, p2)     define a procedure
{
  ...
  RETURN(expression)           hand a value back AND exit immediately
}

result ← procName(a, b)       call it and capture what it returns
procName(a, b)                 call it and ignore what it returns

a ← expression                assign a COPY of the result
DISPLAY(expression)            show it, FOLLOWED BY A SPACE
=  is equality.  ← is assignment.  No == anywhere.

IF(condition) { } ELSE { }     the only two selection forms`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Pseudocode Challenge: Procedures</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>Three problems on <code>PROCEDURE</code> and <code>RETURN</code>. Two translate, one traces &mdash; and the trace is the one that catches people.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Do this on paper.</b> There is nothing to run. On exam day you
            get this notation printed and no computer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="reference">
          <h2>Reference Card</h2>

          <Code code={RefCard} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Exam Notation — what you have so far" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="problems">
          <h2>The Problems</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 1 &mdash; translate</h3>

          <p>Rewrite this in exam notation.</p>

          <Code code={P1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Problem 1" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 2 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={P2} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Problem 2" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <p><b>Careful:</b> the last line calls the procedure again. It does not reuse the first result.</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 3 &mdash; translate</h3>

          <p>Rewrite this in exam notation. One line of it does not translate directly &mdash; say which, and what you did about it.</p>

          <Code code={P3} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Problem 3" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Your three answers, with the output written exactly as it appears. It is collected as <b>Homework Drop 1</b>, together with Question Set 9 and Debug Challenge: Procedures. <b>The drop is worth 4 points</b> for everything in it, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
